 "phase": "P0 (Android): the main thread on the cores faster than the slowest tier",
 "date": "2026-10-10",
 "finding": "while re-measuring R2 (rtr2b, rtr2c) the A12's threads were sampled during the Demo (/proc/<pid>/task/*/stat field 39 once a second): with the render thread busy the scheduler ran the main thread mostly on the slower cluster (CPUs 5–7, 1.8 GHz; CPUs 0–3 run at 2.3 GHz). An experiment with R2, the presenter on CPUs 4–7 and the main thread on 0–3 (exp-r2d, hard-coded) gave Demo main 13.10 -> 12.43 and render 10.40 -> 5.91, vs main 12.74 -> 11.94 and render 12.23 -> 7.94; this step is its main-thread half",
 "change": "CAndroidNative: ntsd_pin_current_thread(mask) (sched_setaffinity on the calling thread) and ntsd_cpu_cluster_mask(fast) (from every CPU's cpuinfo_max_freq: the CPUs faster than the slowest tier, or that tier; 0 when unreadable or all equal). NTSDAndroidApp pins the main thread to the faster cores before the session starts and again on resume (a cpuset move can reset the mask); threads it creates afterwards inherit the mask. Placement changes only speed: the game's results do not depend on which core runs it",
 "placement": "rtp0 during the Demo: local.ntsd.port allowed 0-3 and sampled only on CPUs 0–3; the render queue's workers: one created after the pin allowed 0-3, one older 0-7 (render work still runs on any core)",
