 "review": "independent read-only review: a safe hint — _GNU_SOURCE before every include; bounds right on LP64; any read failure leaves the thread unpinned; the kernel intersects the mask with the cpuset and falls back if the cores go offline, so the thread can never be prevented from running. Applied before the gate: pin to every core faster than the slowest tier (a single prime core would be risky), re-pin on resume, the mask width tied to unsigned long, a shadowed name. Noted: later threads inherit the mask (checked on the device: the render queue's workers created afterwards)"
}
